{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851326-solar-james-bond","id":851326,"title":"Solar James Bond","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-22T13:37:29-07:00","id":851326,"title":"Solar James Bond","content":"Inspired by the Night Caste thread, what Caste would you say fits best with a James Bond inspired Solar? And since I know there are many different versions of the character, please specify which version you're referring. Let's call the one from the original novels the Fleming Bond. Remember that I'm only passingly familiar with the character in any version, so try to be fairly specific with why you've chosen a particular caste for a particular version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T14:46:27-07:00","id":851368,"title":"","content":"I think a good argument could be made for Dawn, as James Bond is kinda a thug. A seductive, good looking and manipulative thug... but in the end, the solution is generally violent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T14:51:29-07:00","id":851371,"title":"","content":"I've only read a couple of the original novels and watched a couple of the movies, but I'm inclined to go with Night in both cases. The Abilities match pretty well and while he does use violence I wouldn't really call him a Dawn. My impression is that he'd rather win by cunning, even if he ends up shooting people a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T15:27:39-07:00","id":851391,"title":"","content":"I've only really read <i>Dr. No</i> and <i>Casino Royale</i>, so I shan't speculate on Fleming Bond.<br /> <br /> Generally, though, I'd <i>expect</i> any Bond-based character to be an Eclipse or Night, though the basic character <i>style</i> really goes with any Caste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T13:03:55-07:00","id":853136,"title":"","content":"I think the Solar version needs to be this Bond.<br /> <img src=\"http://i1.wp.com/www.clutchmagonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/screen-shot-2014-12-21-at-12-55-23-pm.png?w=746\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T19:27:19-07:00","id":853282,"title":"","content":"I think it's essentially the question of:<br /> Is he an action hero?<br /> Or is he a spy?<br /> <br /> If he's an action hero, Dawn, if he's a spy, Night.<br /> Either way, he'll also favour Presence and Socialise, but I wouldn't put him as a social class.<br /> <br /> I'd put him as a Night (but possibly that's because I like the films where he's more a spy):<br /> Caste abilities: Athletics, Awareness, Investigation, Socialise, Stealth<br /> Favoured abilities: Drive(Ride?), Firearms(Archery?), Brawl, Integrity, Presence<br /> He also has Larceny 5 (but not many charms) and a high Melee rating. But he does prefer brawl or firearms.<br /> <br /> To be fair, you could also make him a Dawn with those abilities (and his Supernal would I guess be Firearms).<br /> <br /> Luckily, he no longer needs a very high rating in Linguistics for his vast number of languages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T19:49:56-07:00","id":853288,"title":"","content":"I'd divide this up by the different Bond actors:<br /> <br /> <b>Sean Connery -</b> Night. This Bond usually succeeds by trickery. He's suave and not bad in a fight, but in the end his success comes from outwitting his enemies - not outshooting them or being more persuasive. Focus on the deception-oriented Larceny charms rather than the ones that involve actual physical theft. Probably has Presence, Firearms, and Socialize favored.<br /> <br /> <b>Roger Moore - </b>Night again. More trickery, but also a little more emphasis on gadgets than on fighting - favor Lore or Occult. Max out Larceny - Moore-Bond was great at sucker-punching people.<br /> <br /> <b>Pierce Brosnan - </b>More like an Eclipse, really. Brosnan-Bond relied very heavily on superior technology, the odd temporary ally, and being able to talk his way close to targets. Favor stealth and firearms. Find or make up a charm that lets you have perfect hair no matter what happens to you.<br /> <br /> <b>Daniel Craig - </b>Full-on Dawn. Craig-Bond's approach to problems was pretty much always to go in shooting, or engage in dangerous chases. I will also point out that he rarely succeeded in deceiving anyone and managed to survive failing most of his missions. Favor Resistance and Integrity, because Craig-Bond never dies or gives up even when things actually are hopeless.<br /> <br /> I can't speak for David Niven, George Lazenby, or Timothy Dalton - I didn't watch any of their movies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 03-25-2016, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T19:59:13-07:00","id":853290,"title":"","content":"I'd agree with those categorisations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T08:18:37-07:00","id":853484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851326-solar-james-bond?p=853288#post853288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Daniel Craig - </b>Full-on Dawn. Craig-Bond's approach to problems was pretty much always to go in shooting, or engage in dangerous chases. I will also point out that he rarely succeeded in deceiving anyone and managed to survive failing most of his missions. Favor Resistance and Integrity, because Craig-Bond never dies or gives up even when things actually are hopeless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey hey... he obviously had a Socialize specialization in pretending he cares about women for when he wanted to seduce them for info.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T17:52:48-07:00","id":853770,"title":"","content":"Remember that every Bond needs to favor Drive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T18:41:39-07:00","id":853793,"title":"","content":"There's several options; it depends on your focus.<br /> <br /> Eclipse seems like a strong contender if you're going for the suave, convincing Bond who can seduce any woman and cut to someone's motivation in a few words.<br /> <br /> Night fits the tricky, clever Bond who deceives people and plays the general superspy.<br /> <br /> Dawn for the action-hero Bond who shoots people up without flinching and causes lots of explosions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T16:42:30-07:00","id":854246,"title":"","content":"I'd argue for Night, if you want the classic incarnation of the character. Anybody can use violence to win something, but classic Bond is as much about deceit and trickery. Even his car and his gadgets are meant to trick people into thinking they are normal items.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T14:19:55-07:00","id":855236,"title":"","content":"Elias Tremalion is one of the Night Castes featured in <i>Castebook: Night</i> and is a spy for the Haslanti League. And it'd be difficult for him to be more of a Bond expy than he is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T14:37:10-07:00","id":855249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/851326-solar-james-bond?p=855236#post855236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elias Tremalion is one of the Night Castes featured in <i>Castebook: Night</i> and is a spy for the Haslanti League. And it'd be difficult for him to be more of a Bond expy than he is.</div> </div> </div> </div>They even threw in a reference to Q <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T17:36:52-07:00","id":855379,"title":"","content":"I've built a Dawn to try to emulate the novel Bond, where he is an assassin on Her Majesty's service first and foremost. Lots of Stealth, Socialize and Larceny, then everything else into being able to kill in the first round.<br /> <br /> It's quite effective actually, nobody suspects you (flawlessly impenetrable disguise and Spurious Presence) until you kill someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}